---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';

// MCP discovery page: how AI agents and MCP clients connect to the Percolate
// database. Human-readable and indexable; the machine-readable surface is
// the MCP endpoint itself plus llms.txt.
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Percolate MCP Server — Specialty Coffee Data for AI Agents"
  description="Connect Claude, ChatGPT, Cursor, or any MCP client to the Percolate coffee database: 1,100+ curated coffees with tasting profiles and per-coffee brew recipes."
  path="/mcp"
>
  <main class="page">
    <h1>Percolate for AI agents (MCP)</h1>

    <p>The Percolate MCP server gives AI assistants read-only access to our specialty coffee database: 1,100+ curated coffees with roast, body, acidity, and sweetness profiles, flavor notes, and curated brew recipes (ratio, temperature, grind) per coffee. Ask your AI for coffee recommendations, brewing guidance for a specific bag, or beans similar to ones you love &mdash; and it can answer from real catalog data instead of guessing.</p>

    <h2>Connect in one minute</h2>

    <p><strong>Claude</strong> &mdash; one click, then confirm the connector:</p>
    <p>
      <a
        class="btn"
        href="https://claude.ai/customize/connectors?modal=add-custom-connector&connectorName=Percolate&connectorUrl=https%3A%2F%2Fwmpiabzlcaqyrzxvfihi.supabase.co%2Ffunctions%2Fv1%2Fmcp"
        rel="noopener">Connect to Claude</a>
    </p>

    <p><strong>Claude Desktop</strong> (and other clients that launch local servers) &mdash; add to your MCP config:</p>
    <pre is:raw><code>{
  "mcpServers": {
    "percolate": { "command": "npx", "args": ["-y", "percolate-mcp"] }
  }
}</code></pre>
    <p><strong>Remote clients</strong> (web agents, Cursor, anything that takes a URL) &mdash; use the hosted endpoint, no install or API key:</p>
    <pre><code>https://wmpiabzlcaqyrzxvfihi.supabase.co/functions/v1/mcp</code></pre>

    <h2>What tools does the Percolate MCP server provide?</h2>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Tool</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>search_coffees</code></td><td>Search by name, category, roast, brew method, and price</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>get_coffee</code></td><td>Full tasting profile, pairings, and retailers for one coffee</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>find_similar</code></td><td>Coffees with a similar profile</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>get_recommendations</code></td><td>Picks from flavors, budget, roast, and your brew gear</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>compare_coffees</code></td><td>Side-by-side comparison</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>trending_coffees</code></td><td>What users are adding to collections right now</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>dial_in_suggestion</code></td><td>Curated brew recipe for a specific coffee</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>what_to_brew</code></td><td>A coffee for right now — evenings lean decaf</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2>What can an AI answer with it?</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>&ldquo;Recommend a medium roast with chocolate and nutty notes.&rdquo;</li>
      <li>&ldquo;How should I brew Onyx Monarch on a V60?&rdquo;</li>
      <li>&ldquo;What coffee works for espresso under $20?&rdquo;</li>
      <li>&ldquo;What should I brew tonight?&rdquo;</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Access, privacy, and attribution</h2>
    <p>All tools are read-only and public &mdash; no account, API key, or authentication is required. Requests are rate-limited to 60 calls per minute. Every response includes source attribution and data freshness dates; quote freely with attribution to Percolate (percolateapp.com). Anonymous usage telemetry (tool name, arguments, client name, timing) is logged to operate the service and purged after 90 days; no user identity or conversation content is collected.</p>

    <h2>For developers</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>npm package: <a href="https://www.npmjs.com/package/percolate-mcp">percolate-mcp</a></li>
      <li>GitHub (README, examples): <a href="https://github.com/bguillow-rgb/percolate-mcp">bguillow-rgb/percolate-mcp</a></li>
      <li>Official MCP registry: <code>io.github.bguillow-rgb/percolate</code></li>
      <li>Smithery listing: <a href="https://smithery.ai/servers/bguillow/percolate">smithery.ai/servers/bguillow/percolate</a></li>
    </ul>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
